WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.120
No shirt, these forking actors ought to&nbsp;
have their mother-forking mouths washed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.615
out with god-dang soap. Let's forking do this.
 
 
 &nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.240
Thanks to the extensive research by British gaming&nbsp;
company Buzz Bingo, we can start our list with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.960
Danny McBride at number 10. The curse-counters&nbsp;
over there put McBride’s naughty word film total&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.880
at 136 curse words on screen over the course of&nbsp;
his movie career. Again, that’s according to Buzz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.600
Bingo, but if you can’t trust an internet gambling&nbsp;
site to count curse words, who can you trust?

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.240
It's not surprising that McBride makes the&nbsp;
list, as he is most well-known for raunchy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:40.320
R-rated comedies like Pineapple Express and Tropic&nbsp;
Thunder. McBride even contributed voice acting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.960
Sausage Party, and we really don’t need to&nbsp;
explain Sausage Party any more than that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.920
right? Good. His ranking on this list might&nbsp;
have been even higher had his performances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.600
in several HBO shows, including Eastbound and&nbsp;
Down and The Righteous Gemstones, been taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.880
into consideration. Unfortunately, television&nbsp;
shows weren't counted in this film-focused study.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.920
McBride has become known for&nbsp;
playing pretty horrible characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.320
an archetype that likely contributed to him&nbsp;
getting a spot on this lineup. In The Foot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.520
Fist Way, he plays an incompetent Taekwondo&nbsp;
instructor on a mission to meet his idol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.433
This Is The End sees him as an egotistical actor&nbsp;
who doesn’t get the gravity of what’s going on.

00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:21.434
And he plays a lazy, slobbish prince in "Your Highness."

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:25.440
"Where the f--- was that in Green Hornet, huh?&nbsp;
Jonah, you're f---ing sucking b---s. You're an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.200
Academy Award nominated person, you need to&nbsp;
be f---cking selling that s---, dude."
 
 
 
 &nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.880
Coming in at number nine is Bradley Cooper,&nbsp;
who has uttered a respectable 142 swear words&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.280
over the course of his decades-long career.&nbsp;
Unlike several other actors on this list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.720
Cooper doesn't appear in any of&nbsp;
the top 10 most swear-heavy films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.480
nor does he play any of the most&nbsp;
explicit characters in film history.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.880
In recent years, Cooper has become known for&nbsp;
Oscar-winning dramas like A Star Is Born,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.280
American Hustle, and Silver Linings&nbsp;
Playbook. R-rated dramas like these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.360
have likely contributed to Cooper's place&nbsp;
on the list, but the fact that he's never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.680
starred in a Scorsese or a Tarantino&nbsp;
film certainly docks him a few points.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.320
In addition to his featured dramas, Bradley Cooper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.480
also starred in The Hangover and its&nbsp;
two sequels, a series that undoubtedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.320
contributed a significant number of&nbsp;
curse words to his overall score.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.312
"Alright, what that f---, man? We&nbsp;
gotta get this s--- together, guys!"

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.840
Cooper also voiced the crass Rocket Raccoon in&nbsp;
the Guardians of the Galaxy films, but since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:29.200
Marvel films are almost always PG-13, he wasn't&nbsp;
allowed to go as far as he might have liked.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.040
In fact, Guardians director James Gunn&nbsp;
tweeted that there is unseen footage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.480
Rocket dropping the f-bomb extensively. Gunn&nbsp;
knew he wouldn't be able to use the footage, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.200
filmed it nonetheless. If only Marvel would let&nbsp;
more of their films be as explicit as Deadpool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.560
perhaps Cooper would be higher up on the list.
 
 
 
Like his buddy Danny McBride, Seth Rogen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.560
clinches a spot on the list primarily&nbsp;
because of his work in comedy films.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.680
As number eight, Rogen has dropped a curse&nbsp;
on 143 occasions throughout his career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.160
As with Bradley Cooper, Rogen isn't in&nbsp;
any of the most explicit films out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.920
meaning his swear words have been spread&nbsp;
out over a number of different roles.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.240
Though he has branched out into producing&nbsp;
more recently, Rogen's career kicked off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:14.720
mainly through stoner comedies. After getting&nbsp;
his start on the teen show Freaks and Geeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.801
Rogen starred in raunchy comedies like&nbsp;
Superbad, Knocked Up, and Pineapple Express

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.640
"Except if you're a d--- your whole life,&nbsp;
your next shell will be made of s---,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.029
okay? If you're an a-------. you're&nbsp;
gonna come back as a cockroach."
 
 
 
 
 &nbsp;

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.000
Billy Bob Thornton may not be the first&nbsp;
person you think of in a discussion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.800
about the most explicit actors out there,&nbsp;
but with 100 acting credits to his name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.800
it's not all that surprising he made the&nbsp;
cut. Thornton is number seven on the list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.200
having delivered 145 curse&nbsp;
words over the last few decades.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.680
"This is bulls---. Give me one good reason why&nbsp;
I should even consider doing this right now."

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.366
"Cuz I let 2000 kids spit in my&nbsp;
f---ing face for your a--, that's why."

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.080
While Thornton's character in Bad Santa doesn't&nbsp;
top the list of the most vulgar characters in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.880
