Buzz Bingo folks. Statistically speaking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:27.360
that means that slightly more than 35 out of&nbsp;
every 1,000 words in the film are “bad words”.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.720
"And what f---ing DJ is gonna play his s---?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:35.200
I know every f---ing DJ in this&nbsp;
town. F--- all you losers."

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:40.240
Uncut Gems became so famous for its swearing&nbsp;
that Netflix actually compiled a video of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.480
every f-bomb dropped in the film, ending&nbsp;
up with more than four minutes of footage.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:49.760
You might think that Sandler saves the cursing for&nbsp;
his R rated flicks, and his raunchy PG-13’s are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:54.720
